  "term": "inner dialogue",
  "definition": "Inner dialogue is an internal back-and-forth conversation in the mind, involving linguistic turn-taking between different felt positions or voices within the self. In the source packet, it is described as a spontaneous, persistent experience that can be felt as part of oneself.",
